[agent:bash] databricks registered-models create --help
[agent:result] command: databricks registered-models create --help
[agent:result] stdout: Create a Registered Model.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]   Creates a new registered model in Unity Catalog.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]   File storage for model versions in the registered model will be located in the
[agent:result]   default location which is specified by the parent schema, or the parent
[agent:result]   catalog, or the Metastore.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]   For registered model creation to succeed, the user must satisfy the following
[agent:result]   conditions: - The caller must be a metastore admin, or be the owner of the
[agent:result]   parent catalog and schema, or have the **USE_CATALOG** privilege on the parent
[agent:result]   catalog and the **USE_SCHEMA** privilege on the parent schema. - The caller
[agent:result]   must have the **CREATE MODEL** or **CREATE FUNCTION** privilege on the parent
[agent:result]   schema.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] Usage:
[agent:result]   databricks registered-models create [flags]
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] Flags:
[agent:result]       --browse-only               Indicates whether the principal is limited to retrieving metadata for the associated object through the BROWSE privilege when include_browse is enabled in the request.
[agent:result]       --catalog-name string       The name of the catalog where the schema and the registered model reside.
